# webgl-virgl.flakes: the subtests of WebGL pages that judge.py webgl does
# not judge in the virgl cases, `PATH ERE` a line, PATH as the suite's list
# gives it, or a directory of it ending in `/` for every page under it, and
# ERE an extended regular expression searched for in the subtest's message.
#
# occlusion-query-scissor.html: an ANY_SAMPLES_PASSED query whose draws a
# 0x0 scissor rectangle leaves empty reads 1 in 53 to 64 of the page's 65
# such passes, which ones changing from run to run, in both browsers in the
# Debian guest as on Rach2 (dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md); the page's 454
# other subtests passed in every run and are judged.
conformance2/query/occlusion-query-scissor.html ^pass [0-9]+, result: 1 === expected: 0$
#
# deqp/functional/gles3/texturefiltering/: every case of chunk 4's 103 pages
# fails "Image verification failed" in the Debian guest as on Rach2, and the
# 13 that begin chunk 5 pass in its new browser. The count of subtests
# passed is the verifier's checks of pixels that miss the ideal image, up to
# a case's first failing iteration. Under the testing PC's NVIDIA driver
# 621.24 the Debian guest's run of chunk 4 gives Rach2's counts on the 3D
# pages, which its reference under 621.01 did not, and on the 2D-array and
# cube pages counts that move from run to run, as Rach2's do; with fewer
# pages run before them, four 3D pages pass outright
# (dev-log/84-locks/84-265t.md). A case that fails otherwise is judged, and
# the dEQP-GLES3 cases judge the same filtering case by case. The line stays
# when chunk 4's reference is taken again, since those counts move.
deqp/functional/gles3/texturefiltering/ Image verification failed$
